                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5a319f7b-752e-301d-b27d-8ffc3851466f",
                        "entry_id": "1f8196db-0dc9-3d70-8b93-cb6a8cccb994",
                        "glosses": [
                            "een pijnlijke, hatelijke, satirische vertrekking van het gelaat die doet denken aan een glimlach"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "39084646-8b44-49e5-86da-51ad127cb432",
                                "sense_id": "5a319f7b-752e-301d-b27d-8ffc3851466f",
                                "text": "Een bescheiden sprongetje, een grijnslachje. Jan Smeekens bedankt het publiek en denkt: fuck. Fuckfuckfuck."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b27d4e00-a474-4f0b-8e9c-6fbdb029173e",
                                "sense_id": "5a319f7b-752e-301d-b27d-8ffc3851466f",
                                "text": "Kuzu heeft welbewust zijn eer te grabbel gegooid, hij zou zich moeten schamen. Maar doet dat niet. Hij geniet juist van zijn schaamteloosheid; zijn grijnslach bij elke zin die hij uitspreekt, is die van een slager die graag het rund uitbeent als het nog leeft."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "02f23014-a9a9-4d64-8f7e-49b48e5f61e2",
                                "sense_id": "5a319f7b-752e-301d-b27d-8ffc3851466f",
                                "text": "Langzaam worden de lachuitingen extremer, met wijd opengesperde monden, voor- of achteroverbuigende torso’s en grijnslachen die het gelaat tot angstaanjagende maskers vervormen."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6e6f2686-2b3e-48ec-b892-6f9d9492587e",
                        "source_entry_id": "1f8196db-0dc9-3d70-8b93-cb6a8cccb994",
                        "source_sense_id": "5a319f7b-752e-301d-b27d-8ffc3851466f",
                        "source_sense_description": "een pijnlijke, hatelijke, satirische vertrekking van het gelaat",
                        "target_lang_word": "smirk",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "smirk",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "743881bd-bb12-38a2-a503-1a3358a431a6",
                                        "entry_id": "ff4b5cdf-7672-3c2f-be04-cb9fb701f881",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An uneven, often crooked smile that is insolent, self-satisfied, conceited or scornful."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "56dbbe64-9ba4-319e-8846-def7518a1855",
                                        "entry_id": "ff4b5cdf-7672-3c2f-be04-cb9fb701f881",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A forced or affected smile."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f10ed6f4-41ac-439e-945d-e7fdbc623f10",
                                                "sense_id": "56dbbe64-9ba4-319e-8846-def7518a1855",
                                                "text": "The bride, all smirk and blush, had just entered."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f1808bc2-c5dc-4a27-9b78-0b3be1468e72",
                                                "sense_id": "56dbbe64-9ba4-319e-8846-def7518a1855",
                                                "text": "We sat at a long table with a huge salmon on a platter in the center, prepared Szechuan style. Dad sat at one end of the table, and regaled all present with his stories. In the middle of one convoluted yarn, he rose and went around to the salmon in the center of the table. Using his fingers, he dug an eyeball out of the fish, popped it in his mouth and swallowed it whole as we looked on, aghast. “A real delicacy,” he said, with a boyish smirk."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "smirk",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c920e191-2ff9-34cc-b819-d4d6f8398df5",
                                        "entry_id": "0b95bacd-d25b-37ae-8735-494a54755d12",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To smile in a way that is affected, smug, insolent or contemptuous."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "smirk",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2ada3b42-8512-3312-8e83-c22960613b8c",
                                        "entry_id": "846795bc-4586-3edf-80c5-023ff8180a0f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "smart; spruce; affected; simpering"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5f8a9a88-bf55-49b7-a3cb-13ba2d652680",
                                                "sense_id": "2ada3b42-8512-3312-8e83-c22960613b8c",
                                                "text": "So smirk, so smooth, his pricked Ears."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f8408a05-23cf-4e03-aa99-acd219ee047f",
                        "source_entry_id": "1f8196db-0dc9-3d70-8b93-cb6a8cccb994",
                        "source_sense_id": "5a319f7b-752e-301d-b27d-8ffc3851466f",
                        "source_sense_description": "een pijnlijke, hatelijke, satirische vertrekking van het gelaat",
                        "target_lang_word": "sneer",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "sneer",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2c686dee-3c99-3796-a845-31a653741a95",
                                        "entry_id": "a3ba2378-a96c-317f-b1f3-2eece4055041",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To raise a corner of the upper lip slightly, especially in scorn."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f7814772-d3f4-4346-a6ea-110b18909d21",
                                                "sense_id": "2c686dee-3c99-3796-a845-31a653741a95",
                                                "text": "So General Oakfield's friends taunted him with having been beaten, and Blackeston's friends sneered at him for not having called the general out. Blackeston, a studious and sensitive man, felt the taunts of his friends as only a student can."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1f975399-12d2-3c8f-8fb6-55395636c925",
                                        "entry_id": "a3ba2378-a96c-317f-b1f3-2eece4055041",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To utter with a grimace or contemptuous expression; to say sneeringly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "409cf0dc-9cc6-4a67-9c23-5fe02acb68a2",
                                                "sense_id": "1f975399-12d2-3c8f-8fb6-55395636c925",
                                                "text": "to sneer fulsome lies at a person"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e75933aa-e2b7-47d6-b4a1-387c49b5b8db",
                                                "sense_id": "1f975399-12d2-3c8f-8fb6-55395636c925",
                                                "text": "There was a quick scuffle within the cabin. \"Leave me alone, I say, and git!\" cried the cook. \"Can't I be friendly without you hollerin?\" sneered the miner. \"You wouldn't have been 'lowed to stay round here if it hadn't been for me.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "sneer",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "21761fc0-0ab6-32da-ba21-0e63289e3154",
                                        "entry_id": "b4582e1c-f17b-33ca-8f9a-13d57aeae88e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A facial expression where one slightly raises one corner of the upper lip, generally indicating scorn."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8d8ac7e8-3917-46dc-9baf-a43bedd153c0",
                                                "sense_id": "21761fc0-0ab6-32da-ba21-0e63289e3154",
                                                "text": "Near them, on the sand, / Half sunk, a shattered visage lies, whose frown, / And wrinked lip, and sneer of cold command, / Tell that its sculptor well those passions read"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b53dd644-9bd4-4dc9-baf6-cafdd4887b0f",
                                                "sense_id": "21761fc0-0ab6-32da-ba21-0e63289e3154",
                                                "text": "He supposed then (with a sneer—M. Paul could sneer supremely, curling his lip, opening his nostrils, contracting his eyelids)—he supposed there was but one form of appeal to which I would listen [...]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a43b1dd1-444f-3619-aeb2-8241ad254b20",
                                        "entry_id": "b4582e1c-f17b-33ca-8f9a-13d57aeae88e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A display of contempt; scorn."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8223a22f-c0a3-4302-a097-c56d3ff4afeb",
                                                "sense_id": "a43b1dd1-444f-3619-aeb2-8241ad254b20",
                                                "text": "And wordy attacks against slavery drew sneers from observers which were not altogether undeserved. The authors were compared to doctors who offered to a patient nothing more than invectives against the disease which consumed him."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5a28ef36-161d-4e2c-8375-5a74d09380bf",
                                                "sense_id": "a43b1dd1-444f-3619-aeb2-8241ad254b20",
                                                "text": "It was a casual sneer, obviously one of a long line. There was hatred behind it, but of a quiet, chronic type, nothing new or unduly virulent, and he was taken aback by the flicker of amazed incredulity that passed over the younger man's ravaged face."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4b3059b5-caee-492c-980c-ebe9a3f33f87",
                                                "sense_id": "a43b1dd1-444f-3619-aeb2-8241ad254b20",
                                                "text": "During [Tucker] Carlson’s keynote, he wedged sneers at his critics for crying “racist!” in between racist remarks about [Ilhan] Omar, jeremiads against the media (“I know there’s a bunch of reporters here, so . . . screw you”), and an attack on Elizabeth Warren and her donors (“She’s a tragedy, because she’s now obsessed with racism, which is why the finance world supports her”)—all to gleeful applause."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1a9bea20-f54a-4fff-9faf-9e52e37de19e",
                        "source_entry_id": "1f8196db-0dc9-3d70-8b93-cb6a8cccb994",
                        "source_sense_id": "5a319f7b-752e-301d-b27d-8ffc3851466f",
                        "source_sense_description": "een pijnlijke, hatelijke, satirische vertrekking van het gelaat",
                        "target_lang_word": "grin",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "grin",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "efacd85a-f8e0-3ab7-b039-ac704307ff64",
                                        "entry_id": "b3d6149a-5c56-311f-89f0-f6d8ff8155ca",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A snare; a gin."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "grin",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "58976188-ffe0-342d-bc4c-a21deb565949",
                                        "entry_id": "332f4bdd-1ad3-37eb-b329-f39caf720f06",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A smile in which the lips are parted to reveal the teeth."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "03c703e3-c607-4b60-b922-b3812d929bd9",
                                                "sense_id": "58976188-ffe0-342d-bc4c-a21deb565949",
                                                "text": "When the ceremony was finished a wide grin broke across his face, and it was that grin she saw, relieved and happy all at once."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "05a6199a-3ce2-4a98-8880-0ed9f355d2f8",
                                                "sense_id": "58976188-ffe0-342d-bc4c-a21deb565949",
                                                "text": "When my son appeared at the door the next day with his schoolbag on his back, the Professor broke into a wide grin and opened his arms to embrace him."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "grin",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5c5093b9-054f-3ee5-891a-008c7d0c3aa0",
                                        "entry_id": "e269ee4b-f7aa-3e85-ab2c-a7757233515f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To smile, parting the lips so as to show the teeth."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d5645d43-7dc1-4f4e-84b3-e2b9cd4c78d4",
                                                "sense_id": "5c5093b9-054f-3ee5-891a-008c7d0c3aa0",
                                                "text": "Why do you grin? Did I say something funny?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a17c7694-b2f7-4941-a669-6df729dfc9df",
                                                "sense_id": "5c5093b9-054f-3ee5-891a-008c7d0c3aa0",
                                                "text": "‘No,’ said Luke, grinning at her. ‘You're not dull enough! […] What about the kid's clothes? I don't suppose they were anything to write home about, but didn't you keep anything? A bootee or a bit of embroidery or anything at all?’"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8e6ec1b2-5772-3673-bb1f-1788ea815c44",
                                        "entry_id": "e269ee4b-f7aa-3e85-ab2c-a7757233515f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To express by grinning."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b215d8a8-13b5-4b43-94d8-e20a8870349e",
                                                "sense_id": "8e6ec1b2-5772-3673-bb1f-1788ea815c44",
                                                "text": "She grinned pleasure at his embarrassment."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2ef97add-a6fd-4569-a318-c39369babb49",
                                                "sense_id": "8e6ec1b2-5772-3673-bb1f-1788ea815c44",
                                                "text": "Grinned horrible a ghastly smile."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9c388157-e64e-409e-a5ff-de634439a25b",
                                                "sense_id": "8e6ec1b2-5772-3673-bb1f-1788ea815c44",
                                                "text": "\"Mid-Lent, and the Enemy grins,\" remarked Selwyn as he started for church with Nina and the children. Austin, knee-deep in a dozen Sunday supplements, refused to stir; poor little Eileen was now convalescent from grippe, but still unsteady on her legs; her maid had taken the grippe, and now moaned all day: \"Mon dieu! Mon dieu! Che fais mourir!\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0668f0ca-c970-33c8-999c-a2bde894b932",
                                        "entry_id": "e269ee4b-f7aa-3e85-ab2c-a7757233515f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To show the teeth, like a snarling dog."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated",
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b1b34602-2e0b-460f-93c3-8848dc5882d9",
                                                "sense_id": "0668f0ca-c970-33c8-999c-a2bde894b932",
                                                "text": "The pangs of death do make him grin."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "690254e5-c703-4ebd-9c5d-cadf662ef5f9",
                                                "sense_id": "0668f0ca-c970-33c8-999c-a2bde894b932",
                                                "text": "They burned the old gun that used to stand in the dark corner up in the garret, close to the stuffed fox that always grinned so fiercely. Perhaps the reason why he seemed in such a ghastly rage was that he did not come by his death fairly. And why else was he put away up there out of sight?—and so magnificent a brush as he had too."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "21e5d0c2-11d7-3dff-9767-ce429a375c85",
                                        "entry_id": "e269ee4b-f7aa-3e85-ab2c-a7757233515f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To grin as part of producing a particular facial expression, such as a smile or sneer."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "656bb01e-b378-4d99-9d90-e4e18aea7a85",
                                                "sense_id": "21e5d0c2-11d7-3dff-9767-ce429a375c85",
                                                "text": "He grinned a broad smile when I told him the result."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "93731f34-326f-486b-90ec-08153617b423",
                                                "sense_id": "21e5d0c2-11d7-3dff-9767-ce429a375c85",
                                                "text": "He grinned a cruel sneer when I begged him to stop."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
